    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pū^trēdo</span></b> ,
			ĭnis, f.
		putreo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>rottenness</i>, <i>putridity</i>
			(late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnerum,</span>”
				<i>festering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 222, 37</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 9, 31</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 17, 57</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. 2, 44, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 4, 3, 26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aufer meorum putredines peccatorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 5, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
